atlas capability

architecture capability-lattice
  canonical_name CapabilityLattice
  family capability
  domain Capability
  layer capability
  semantic_question What does the system actually have, by estate and law, as real callable binaries?
  purpose The one anti-amnesia mechanism the architecture blesses as non-universal: classify every probed binary into its primary estate and the computational law it preserves.
  maturity implemented
  node_types Capability
  node_types Estate
  node_types Law
  edge_types classified_into
  edge_types preserves_law
  state_types defined
  state_types resolvable
  state_types callable
  state_types health_probed
  state_types workload_proven
  forbidden_inference a family name -> the estate is only that (BonfyreNet is not only networking)
  forbidden_inference classified into an estate -> cannot span estates
  command BonfyreCapability
  source_path 10-Code/BonfyreControlPlane/estate_catalog.py
  source_path 10-Code/BonfyreControlPlane/capability_catalog.py
  source_path 10-Code/BonfyreControlPlane/probe_native_capabilities.py
  source_path 10-Code/BonfyreControlPlane/probe_native_commands.py
  witness 10-Code/BonfyreControlPlane/tests/test_capability_catalog.py
  source_lineage bonfyre operating model plural-fabric

architecture discipl-composition
  canonical_name DisCIPLCompositionGraph
  consumes CommandAdvertisement
  family capability
  domain Capability / Composition
  layer capability/composition
  semantic_question What typed chain of transforms bridges this source family to this destination family, and at what cost?
  purpose The native composition calculus: contracts with success_prior, transform_cost, semantic_loss. Never reimplemented in Python -- the engine is called.
  maturity implemented
  node_types ContractRow
  node_types Family
  edge_types transforms
  edge_types bridges
  forbidden_inference a proposed chain -> a runnable chain (binding is separate)
  computational_form fused
  command BonfyreDiscipl
  source_path 10-Code/BonfyreControlPlane/capability_closure.py
  source_path 10-Code/BonfyreControlPlane/command_pipeline_seed.py
  witness 10-Code/BonfyreControlPlane/tests/test_capability_closure.py
  source_lineage capability closure essay

architecture capability-closure
  owns Capability
  derived Capability
  consumes ExecutionReceipt
  consumes Credential
  publishes Capability
  canonical_name CapabilityClosureGraph
  family capability
  domain Capability / Execution
  layer capability/execution
  semantic_question Can this composed chain be bound to real binaries, gated by the frontier, and run?
  purpose Compose (DisCIPL) -> bind to real binaries (estate/law) -> gate (proof frontier) -> select form -> execute. Execution is evidence: a hop that ran a real workload earns workload_proven.
  maturity measured
  node_types ExecutionOrganism
  node_types Hop
  node_types FormSelection
  edge_types binds_to
  edge_types gated_by
  edge_types promotes
  internal_calculus form selection (durable|fused|trajectory|coupled) by hop laws
  invariant a blocked organism refuses at the execution boundary; the gate is not advisory
  invariant a command that ran a real workload earns workload_proven, cited by a receipt
  forbidden_inference composition allowed -> touching a proven layer allowed
  forbidden_inference bound to a binary -> executes to completion (needs substrate inputs)
  computational_form fused
  computational_form durable
  command BonfyreDiscipl
  command BonfyreFPQ
  source_path 10-Code/BonfyreControlPlane/capability_closure.py
  witness 10-Code/BonfyreControlPlane/tests/test_fpq_closure.py
  witness 10-Code/BonfyreControlPlane/tests/test_capability_closure.py
  source_lineage capability closure essay
